course: dictionary
lesson: 1281
title: Butler: a servant in a big house
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a job. A butler is the chief male servant in a large, rich house, and he looks after the wine, the dining room and the other servants.
explain: Read the clues around the word. In «the trap-door that led up into the butler's pantry», the word pantry is near the word butler, so the butler's pantry is a place in the house where he works. In «the passage comes up under the butler's pantry, right next to the dining-hall!», the pantry is right next to the room where people eat.
explain: Words can also carry a picture of a character. Sam and Jake shout «PO-TAH-TO» like a posh butler, so they are copying the way a butler might talk. When you read about a butler, think about how he behaves: in stories he is often polite and calm.
fact: A butler is a noun: a butler, butlers.
fact: «Butler» means the chief male servant in a large, rich house.
fact: A butler looks after the wine, the dining room and the other servants.
fact: Butler is also a surname, the name of a family.
fact: In stories and films, a butler is often polite and calm, and in mystery stories people joke «the butler did it».
exercise: «They come to a trap-door, push it up together and climb into the butler's pantry.» What is a butler? | A pet dog kept in a kitchen | A chef who cooks in a café | *The chief male servant in a large, rich house
exercise: In a large, rich house, what does a butler look after? | *The wine, the dining room and the other servants | The garden and the car | The school and the library
exercise: Which of these can butler also be? | A bus driver | A kind of cake | *A surname, the name of a family
test: Sam and Jake shout «PO-TAH-TO» like a posh butler. Why do they copy a butler's voice? | Because they have lost their voices | *Because it is a joke about how posh butlers talk | Because they are going to cook dinner
test: In stories and films, which word best describes a butler? | Always asleep | Rude and noisy | *Polite and calm
exam: «The passage comes up under the butler's pantry, right next to the dining-hall!» Where is the butler's pantry? | *Next to the dining-hall | In the garden shed | Under the sea | Up a tall tree
